//==
// # A grid with its nodes evaluated once: types (TKT-502, chunk QF3)
//
// Layer 05-face-meshing. QuadGrid evaluated each cell's four corners (about four evaluations per
// node), tested each cell's keep rule twice and built the split triangles of kept cells only to
// drop them; the keep gate then evaluated every corner again for each rendering triangle. A grid
// now carries one position per parameter point, read by the cell rule and the gate.

// A grid in parameter space with the surface position of every one of its points, in the same
// order: Positions[i] is the surface at Grid.Points[i].
type PositionedGrid
{
    Grid: UvTriangulation;
    Positions: Array<Point3D>;
}
